    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a03d0d2b",
      "@type": "TargetCommunity",
      "instance_name": "audience_id",
      "label": "audience description",
      "description": "The target community is individuals who hold or are exposed to racialized assumptions about Black family structures, particularly those who may be influenced by or reinforce stereotypes that Black children are less capable of understanding traditional familial roles. The meme is designed to provoke a reaction from audiences who interpret the question as morally urgent or potentially harmful, leveraging the visual of a joyful Black child to frame a racially charged narrative. This audience may include people who subscribe to or are influenced by anti-Black stereotypes, such as the assumption that non-traditional family structures are inherently unstable or morally ambiguous, and who may use the meme to reinforce or critique such beliefs.",
